rt_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"Werkhuizenstraat","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Sint-Jans-Molenbeek","address_line1":"Werkhuizenstraat, 17","address_line2":"1080 Sint-Jans-Molenbeek","description_web":"Vandaag de dag wonen meer dan 180 nationaliteiten samen in Brussel. Het MigratieMuseumMigration geeft de verhalen van de eerste generatiegastarbeiders, van de vroegste bewoners van het Klein Kasteeltje, van de expats, de oorlogsvluchtelingen, de Europeanen die zich vrij bewegen binnen de EU en vele anderen een permanente thuis. Het is een warme omgeving waar bezoekers via herinneringen en kunst op ontdekking gaan in Brussel en in het leven van anderen.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"Today, more than 180 nationalities live together in Brussels. The MigratieMuseumMigration gives a permanent home to the stories of the first generation of guest workers, of the earliest inhabitants of the Petit-Cha\u0302teau, of the expats, the war refugees, the Europeans who move freely within the EU and many others. It is a warm environment where visitors can discover Brussels and the lives of others through memories and souvenirs. Above all, it is a museum with plenty of room to share your own story.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":nu